# `A ⊑ ∃u.⊤` with `Range(u,G)` and the consumer `∃u.G ⊑ W`, so `A ⊑ W`.
#
# Until #435 this was the report-only vehicle: the saturator lowered `∃u.⊤` to a
# subsumer-less ⊤-witness, `Range(u)=G` never reached it, `build_model` reported
# `LabelNotClosed`, and (with the consumer) classify missed `A ⊑ W` under a pure-EL
# completeness claim. That subsumer-lessness was recorded as a design decision; #435
# showed it was a defect. The witness now stands for the set of `u`-successors and
# carries `Range(u)`, so the label closes and `A ⊑ W` is derived.
#
# Konclude and HermiT agree on the one non-trivial row.
provenance: konclude-v0.7.0-1138
subclass: A W
